{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Is there yet</b> — The heh is for inquiry, and because of the guttural sign it opens as is the rule, and this is like: העוד אביכם חי. And behold, the seed was already sown in the ground, and the meaning is: you have no places for granaries besides the מגורה, to put grain in the houses, like נהרסו ממגורות, because since the hail struck them they had only a little. And behold, the meaning: if I strike you this year, you will die. And behold, when you began to found the House, then the blessing begins in everything." "<b>From the day the temple was founded</b> — I will bless, and this is מן היום הזה ומעלה said above. And he mentioned the fruit of the tree, those mentioned being the vine and the fig and the pomegranate and the olive; and the meaning [is that] it did not put forth blossom nor leaf, and a fortiori fruit — until now it has not put forth."], :book :haggai, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Haggai" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/hagai"] ["Ibn Ezra on Haggai -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/hagai"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:37.205066955Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}